  "body": "The Sodick LN2W post can write the control's wire offset (#4076): `G41` / `G42 Hnnn` before the lead-in and `G40` on the lead-out. The post reads a `COMP` record in the stream.\n\nThe app does not write a `COMP` record for a Wire Contour. `crates/app/src/posting_wire.rs` posts the wire-centre path and states compensation off. So no LN2W program with offset can come from the app.\n\nWork:\n\n1. Add a compensation mode to Wire Contour: \"in computer\" (the default, as now), \"in control\" and \"wear\".\n2. For \"in control\", generate the part contour with a straight lead-in and lead-out that are at least the offset radius long. Write `COMP` records around each pass, with the radius of each pass.\n3. Decide how the wire laws (kerf, threading, slug) judge a path that the control offsets (#1498). The register value is set at the control, so the laws must judge the path with the stated radius.\n4. Add an MCP tool or parameter for the mode (`area:mcp`), or file `MCP: <command>`.\n5. Add goldens for the square and the 2-axis parts with offset on, rough plus skims (item 4 of #4076).\n\nDone means: the app posts an LN2W program with control-side offset from a Wire Contour, the wire laws judge it, and the existing goldens do not change.\n\nRefs #4076. Safety floor: this changes posted G-code and a gouge check.\n",
